    "title": "Take an Exam with Proctor Desktop",
    "description": "Get Proctor Desktop ready, start your Attempt, keep your work saved, get back on track after an interruption, and submit safely.",
    "href": "/candidate/",
    "searchText": "take an exam with proctor desktop get proctor desktop ready, start your attempt, keep your work saved, get back on track after an interruption, and submit safely. take an exam with proctor desktop you can only take an exam in proctor desktop. your copy of desktop must be a compatible version, and it must have a session tied to its registered key. you can't start an attempt from an ordinary browser session or with a copied bearer token. the server, the sign-in page for authorizing desktop, and the api are ready. the desktop app's code isn't in this repository, so this guide describes the states your attempt can be in and what you can safely do in each. it doesn't guess at the exact labels on desktop's screens or show made-up screenshots. your exam, step by step 1. prepare and enter from candidate exam activity, once desktop has passed its compatibility check and you have authorized it. 2. keep your workspace and participation up to date while desktop confirms that the server has saved every change. 3. learn how the exam browser works and what it records before you follow links to outside reference material. 4. submit, or get going again after a correction, a pause, a disconnection, a suspension or a sync conflict. 5. read your result once it has been released. the result doesn't show private evidence, decisions or manager notes. what the status on your exam card means an exam activity card helps you find your way to the right exam. it is not a lasting promise that you will be let in. a card can show a sitting as upcoming, available, in progress, submitted, result available or past. it offers only the actions that are safe right now, such as enter, resume or view result. when you enter, proctor checks everything again: your class membership, the state of the sitting, whether your desktop build is compatible, your desktop registration, and your current session. proctor delivers programming exams securely and records signals about exam integrity. it doesn't decide your grade, score, rubric, pass or fail, or whether you did anything wrong."
